requirements.expected_result:
Exactly this string, with these line breaks, backticks, parentheses and full stops, and no prefix of any kind: "GitLab refused the login (401 Unauthorized) for {host}: the token glab signs in with is missing or expired.

{detail}

Sign back in with `glab auth login --hostname {host}` (or export a valid GITLAB_TOKEN), then ask for the merge again. The branch `{branch}` is already pushed, so the team's work is safe." {host} is the remote web URL's host or the literal "your GitLab host" when that is unknown, and it appears TWICE, once in the first sentence and once inside the backticked command. {branch} is the SOURCE branch, backticked. {detail} is glab's own message and is interpolated raw, on its own paragraph, between two blank lines. GITLAB_TOKEN is upper case and unbackticked. The word order, the "(401 Unauthorized)" parenthetical and the closing reassurance are part of the string and must not be reworded or reflowed.

